  "body": "Part of #1065 (the Rust SDK slice; the issue stays open for the second SDK and the component-model/WIT decision, both Drew-owned per the triage on the issue). Queue task 13926.\n\n## What this adds\n\n**`pkgs/id/examples/rust-world` — `plaza-sdk`, the Rust guest SDK.** A pure Rust program implements the `World` trait (`init`/`update`/`view`, optional `layout`/`records`/`wants`/`snapshot`/`restore`) and `plaza_guest!` emits all 14 documented Plaza ABI v1 exports with the exact signatures from `examples/roc-world/ABI.md`: model as an opaque pointer, host inputs in `plaza_alloc` memory freed by `plaza_free`, one shared output slot, snapshot/restore as a total pair. Helper modules equal the Roc platform libraries:\n\n- `screen` = Screen.roc — cell grid, `boxed`, plain text, and the versioned screen JSON (the Roc `expect` values are reproduced byte-for-byte in tests)\n- `json` = RocJson.roc — bounded decode (64 KiB / depth 64), number lexemes preserved, first-key `get`, validating encode\n- `grid` = RocGrid.roc — total, bounds-checked row-major grids\n- `cap` = RocCap.roc — `r<n>` request sessions, request-document builders, result routing\n- `text` = RocText.roc — total text helpers\n\n**`pkgs/id/examples/rust-counter` — the playable example.** Twin of `roc-counter`: trimmed `inc` increments, boxed 20x3 `count=N` screen, layout widening at 30 columns, `{\"count\":N}` records, `{}` wants, decimal snapshot with total restore. `build.sh` rebuilds the checked-in `counter.wasm` (`wasm32-unknown-unknown`); the module exports exactly `memory` + the 14 `plaza_*` functions and has no imports.\n\n**Conformance:** `rust-counter` joins `CONFORMANCE_MODULES` in `pkgs/id/src/sandbox.rs`, so the F12.7 suite — documented export signatures vs ABI.md, ABI version 1, snapshot/restore byte-identical round-trip, records/wants schema validity — now exercises a Rust guest end to end.\n\n## Verification (laptop)\n\n- `cargo test` in `rust-world`: 9 passed. In `rust-counter`: 2 passed.\n- `cargo test --lib sandbox::` in `pkgs/id`: 36 passed, including all five `conformance_*` tests with the rust-counter fixture.\n- PR checks were QUEUED at open time (fleet CI stall); merging under standing merge authority on this verification.\n\n## Not in this slice\n\nThe AssemblyScript-vs-Zig second SDK and the Wasm component-model/WIT direction — Drew-owned decisions recorded on #1065. The SDK README states this explicitly: the SDK targets the landed ABI v1 module contract, and its helper APIs do not depend on the raw boundary, so a future component binding can sit under the same `World` trait.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796778216&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7891&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7891&signature=ad6a07f3ca0d0899e83a9c3a336562c3577b27d8c9214ed0f8cd03d02daac8d6\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7891?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
